bhyve: qemu_fwcfg: memory-mapped interface, DMA and writable files

fw_cfg was only reachable through the two I/O ports, so only on amd64.
Add the memory-mapped interface that QEMU's "virt" machines have (data
register, big-endian selector, DMA address), for platforms without I/O
ports: a platform asks for it with qemu_fwcfg_enable_mmio(base) before
qemu_fwcfg_init().

The DMA interface comes with it (the ID item says so): firmware reads
large files such as ACPI tables in one request instead of a byte per
exit, and it is the only way a guest can write.  A file added with
qemu_fwcfg_add_file_writable() gets the guest's writes and a callback.

